---
description: Never hardcode user-visible UI text; use Fluent via getString
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,ftl,xhtml}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Localization

Do not add hardcoded user-visible English (labels, titles, placeholders, aria-text, tooltips, progress copy, empty states, menu items). Put the string in Fluent and look it up.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button title="Lock page">Lock</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button title={getString("page-lock")}>{getString("page-lock")}</button>
```

```ftl
# addon/locale/en-US/addon.ftl — then the same key in every locale folder
page-lock = Lock page
```

- **Keys:** kebab-case in `addon/locale/en-US/addon.ftl` (this is the bundle `getString` loads). Copy the key into **every** `addon/locale/<code>/addon.ftl`. Do **not** start ids with the `addonRef` from `package.json` — the build already prefixes them, and a double prefix looks up nothing.
- **JS/TSX:** `getString("key")` or `getString("key", { args: { name } })`. Safe in Preact render.
- **Prefs XHTML:** `data-l10n-id` + `preferences.ftl`.
- **Variables:** `{ $name }` in FTL, never concatenate sentences in code.
- **Call `getString` at render/use time**, not at module load (`initLocale` has not run yet).
- **Product name** in `package.json` `config.addonName` stays untranslated.
- Locale folders match Zotero: `de` not `de-DE`; `ar` not `ar-SA`; `pt-BR`, `es-ES`, `fr-FR`, …
- Details: `AGENTS.md`.
